.TH mnnn-net-config 1  "mnnn-net-config 2.9.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-net\-config \- Show or change network settings
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn net config\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-listen\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-mdns\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-autostart\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-bootstrap\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-bootstrap\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or change network settings
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
How this node introduces itself
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Replace the listen addresses (repeatable; \\"default\\" for all interfaces)
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mdns\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
Look for peers on the local network
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-autostart\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
Start the node when the TUI opens (on by default)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\fR \fI<known|anyone>\fR
Connect on its own with `known` nodes only (default) or `anyone`
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-bootstrap\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Add a bootstrap node (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-bootstrap\fR
Remove all bootstrap nodes first
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.9.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
